WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:02.650
Speaker 1: Last week I received an e-mail.

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:07.650
From a right wing viewer saying, you know,
David, you cite these high approval ratings

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:13.749
that Joe Biden supposedly has, but every time
I look at Joe Biden's live streams on YouTube,

00:00:13.749 --> 00:00:16.209
it has thousands of dislikes.

00:00:16.209 --> 00:00:21.440
How could Joe Biden really be that popular
if he has so many dislikes on YouTube?

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.830
Now, of course, this is very much like the
people who were saying in 20/20 during the

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.420
Democratic primary.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:33.880
Bernie Sanders is so much more popular than
Joe Biden on Twitter and he's so much more

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.800
popular on Reddit.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.820
How could Bernie Sanders possibly lose?

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:45.370
And as we quickly learned in 2020, Twitter
read tweets, Reddit upvotes and Facebook likes

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:48.180
and dislikes and YouTube likes and dislikes.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.550
It's not the real world.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:55.510
We do actually have, however, real world polling
data about Joe Biden's presidency so far.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:01.309
And as Joe Biden is approaching 100 days in
office, his approval at this point is surpassing

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:09.280
George W. Bush's Bill Clinton's George H.W.
Bush's by a tiny bit, basically a tie and

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.780
by a huge margin margin Donald Trump's approval
at this point in time.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:21.031
This is new data from the Pew Research Center,
which has Joe Biden right now at 59 percent

00:01:21.031 --> 00:01:22.290
approval.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:26.619
At this point in Donald Trump's presidency,
Trump was polling 39 percent.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:29.260
It's a 20 point gap.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:30.580
It's not even close.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:35.920
And remember that Donald Trump never even
hit 50 percent approval for a single day during

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.420
his presidency.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:42.869
Barack Obama was slightly better than Biden
at 61 percent within the margin of error.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.060
George W. Bush was at 55.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.870
Bill Clinton was at just 49.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:51.200
George H.W. Bush basically within the margin
of error at 58.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:58.869
And we have in the first April of Ronald Reagan's
presidency, Reagan pulled the highest at 67

00:01:58.869 --> 00:01:59.900
percent.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.479
How could this be?

00:02:01.479 --> 00:02:08.670
How could Joe Biden be polling so well, despite,
again, dislikes on his YouTube live streams?

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:15.280
Because the Internet is not real life, most
working people are not taking time out of

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:20.430
their day to dislike a Joe Biden live stream
on YouTube in order to make Biden look bad.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:24.830
They're working and then they're looking at
did he do covid stimulus?

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.110
What's going on with vaccination?

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:31.080
And in fact, when you ask the question, where
is the approval coming from, it's coming from

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.060
the same places as in February and March.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.629
Joe Biden has 72 percent approval on managing
vaccine distribution.

00:02:37.629 --> 00:02:43.400
Joe Biden has 55 percent approval among Republicans
on vaccine distribution.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:48.860
Biden has stronger approval than Trump in
terms of is he behaving in a way that is appropriate

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:51.700
for a president of the United States to behave?

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:56.630
And the one point nine trillion dollar covid
stimulus package, which every Republican in

00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:03.500
the House and Senate voted against, is popular
with two thirds of the country, either strongly

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:07.340
or somewhat approving of the covid stimulus.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.870
That is a big deal.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:12.530
You don't get to 67 percent with just Democrats.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:17.590
And remember that that's not you know, not
a single one of these Republican elected officials

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:21.030
in the House or in the Senate voted for the
bill.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:27.390
Now, in terms of the next few months, if the
vaccine rollout continues, if cases resume

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:32.840
a downward trend, if things go the way that
the highly vaccinated countries like Israel

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:39.490
and the UK are seeing things go, cases plunging,
deaths plunging, things opening.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:44.010
This could actually turn around for Joe Biden
for the worse, and you might be saying, well,

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:47.430
hold on, if things keep improving, how could
it get worse for Joe Biden?

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:51.349
And this is why Republicans and right wing
media have done one thing.

00:03:51.349 --> 00:03:55.379
I don't want to say they've done it well,
but they've done it successfully from their

00:03:55.379 --> 00:03:56.709
point of view.

00:03:56.709 --> 00:04:01.989
Fox News and Newsmax and other right wing
media, in coordination with Republican elected

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:06.769
officials, have successfully turned attention
to immigration.

00:04:06.769 --> 00:04:12.160
And when Pew asked people what are the big
problems right now in the United States, the

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:17.099
number of Americans now saying immigration,
illegal immigration is a big problem has gone

00:04:17.099 --> 00:04:22.089
from just 28 percent in June, up to forty
eight percent this month.

00:04:22.089 --> 00:04:25.409
That's a 20 percent, 20 percentage point jump.

00:04:25.409 --> 00:04:27.210
And that is potentially huge.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:30.580
They realize this is Republicans now and right
wing media.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:33.939
They realized Biden is doing well, uncovered.

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:36.189
Biden is doing well on vaccines.

00:04:36.189 --> 00:04:40.099
Biden got a popular stimulus bill done with
no Republican support.

00:04:40.099 --> 00:04:45.689
So they are taking the approach of pointing
to something else, the manufactured crisis

00:04:45.689 --> 00:04:47.860
at the border, and it is actually working.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:51.409
So this is the potential challenge ahead for
Joe Biden.

00:04:51.409 --> 00:04:56.750
And the truth is that no matter what he does,
Republicans will say he's failing on immigration.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:58.620
This is what Republicans do to Democrats.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:01.159
No matter what Democrats do on guns.

00:05:01.159 --> 00:05:03.599
Republicans say Democrats are trying to take
your guns.

00:05:03.599 --> 00:05:09.689
And no matter what Democrats do on immigration,
Republicans say Democrats are welcoming dangerous

00:05:09.689 --> 00:05:12.360
illegals into the country.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:14.460
And this is going to be a test for Biden.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:15.819
And we will see what he can do with it.

00:05:15.819 --> 00:05:20.189
It's sort of a it's a problem of Biden's own
own making.

00:05:20.189 --> 00:05:21.710
It's not an avoidable one.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:29.379
But the better he does on the pandemic and
the more quickly his management of vaccination

00:05:29.379 --> 00:05:35.059
helps us get out of the pandemic, the more
of an opportunity there is for people to take

00:05:35.059 --> 00:05:39.860
their eye off that ball and to have their
attention focused on whatever else Republicans

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:40.860
are pointing to.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.169
And right now, that's illegal immigration.

00:05:42.169 --> 00:05:45.360
They have nothing else that's even remotely
policy oriented.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.309
Of course, they're lying about what's going
on, as we've covered before, but it doesn't

00:05:49.309 --> 00:05:50.309
matter.

00:05:50.309 --> 00:05:52.300
It's working and we see it in the polling
data.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.990
So this will be a challenge for Joe Biden.

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:57.169
The better he does on the pandemic, the more
he's going to have to deal with this.

00:05:57.169 --> 00:05:58.979
And we know what the right wing playbook is.

00:05:58.979 --> 00:06:00.849
We saw it with Bill Clinton.

00:06:00.849 --> 00:06:02.179
We saw it under Barack Obama.

00:06:02.179 --> 00:06:03.490
The playbook is the same one.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:04.619
It's an effective playbook.

00:06:04.619 --> 00:06:06.650
That's why they keep going back to it.

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:12.689
We will have more on this story and this polling
data for you on The David Pakman Show Instagram

00:06:12.689 --> 00:06:13.689
page.

00:06:13.689 --> 00:06:17.050
You can find us on Instagram at David Pakman
show.

